# Eclipse Mosquitto Password File — TEMPLATE ONLY
# DO NOT COMMIT REAL HASHES OR CREDENTIALS TO SOURCE CONTROL
#
# This file documents the expected username structure for the development broker.
# The real password hash file (`pwfile`) is NOT tracked in git (.gitignored).
#
# To generate the real `pwfile` for local development:
#   1. Copy .env.example to .env and set MQTT_* credentials.
#   2. Run: npm run mqtt:pwfile
#   3. Restart the broker: docker compose restart mqtt-broker
#
# Expected users:
#   gateway_user          — IoT Gateway Service (read/write agriculture/#)
#   device_esp32_001      — Development Device 1 (isolated to own topic namespace)
#   device_node_002       — Development Device 2 (isolated to own topic namespace)
#   unauthorized_device   — Test-only device for ACL denial verification
#
# Credentials are derived from environment variables:
#   MQTT_GATEWAY_USERNAME / MQTT_GATEWAY_PASSWORD
#   MQTT_DEV1_USERNAME    / MQTT_DEV1_PASSWORD
#   MQTT_DEV2_USERNAME    / MQTT_DEV2_PASSWORD
#   MQTT_UNAUTH_USERNAME  / MQTT_UNAUTH_PASSWORD
#
# See: .env.example and scripts/mqtt-config.ts for variable names.
# See: scripts/generate-mqtt-pwfile.ts for the generation logic.
